1
00:00:05,533 --> 00:00:12,433
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:33,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,767 --> 00:00:35,867
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,633 --> 00:00:41,800
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:44,033 --> 00:00:45,333
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:46,400
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:47,533
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:47,533 --> 00:00:48,900
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:51,433 --> 00:00:52,533
[GUNSHOT]

10
00:00:53,133 --> 00:00:54,333
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:54,333 --> 00:00:55,800
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:57,467 --> 00:00:58,667
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,667 --> 00:01:00,667
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:03,333
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:07,067
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:08,733 --> 00:01:09,900
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,633 --> 00:01:12,133
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:12,133 --> 00:01:13,767
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,767 --> 00:01:15,033
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,800
<i>Mr. Chan has consented
to serve as a witness.</i>

21
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:24,567
<i> I will get rid of Mr. Chan.</i>

22
00:01:24,567 --> 00:01:26,300
<i> Now is the time</i>

23
00:01:26,300 --> 00:01:29,033
<i>for you to get rid
of Samantha Jacinto.</i>

24
00:01:29,033 --> 00:01:30,967
<i> I just wanted to tell you
something.</i>

25
00:01:30,967 --> 00:01:32,167
<i> I was suspended.</i>

26
00:01:32,167 --> 00:01:34,500
You tarnished the Jacinto name!

27
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:35,933
<i> You are a disgrace!</i>

28
00:01:35,933 --> 00:01:38,100
I do everything to prove to you

29
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:40,200
<i>that I deserve to be
your daughter too.</i>

30
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:41,400
<i> Sometimes I wish...</i>

31
00:01:41,433 --> 00:01:43,100
it was you who was gone instead.

32
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:45,367
<i> Ricardo!</i>

33
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:49,967
<i> It's likely they abducted
Mister Babot and the others...</i>

34
00:01:49,967 --> 00:01:53,000
<i>...to harvest their organs
to be sold to foreigners.</i>

35
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,167
<i> We promise you that we will
find Mister Babot.</i>

36
00:01:56,167 --> 00:01:58,667
<i>I know where they were taken.
I'll take you there.</i>

37
00:01:58,667 --> 00:02:00,367
Are you sure we can trust Edwin?

38
00:02:00,367 --> 00:02:02,233
<i>We have no other option
but to trust him</i>

39
00:02:02,233 --> 00:02:04,433
<i>if we want to find
Mister Babot and the others.</i>

40
00:02:09,267 --> 00:02:16,167
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

41
00:02:24,833 --> 00:02:26,267
RJ, I'm sorry.

42
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:29,000
I'm sorry because I'm the one

43
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,033
who brought bad luck
to our family.

44
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:34,867
Because of me...

45
00:02:35,833 --> 00:02:38,833
I gave our father a wound
that I can never erase.

46
00:02:38,833 --> 00:02:40,033
[SNIFFLES]

47
00:02:41,467 --> 00:02:42,633
Im sorry.

48
00:02:42,633 --> 00:02:44,833
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

49
00:02:44,833 --> 00:02:47,000
I'm sorry you died
because of me.

50
00:02:49,567 --> 00:02:50,767
[SOBBING]

51
00:02:51,467 --> 00:02:58,300
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

52
00:02:58,667 --> 00:03:00,700
[SOBBING, SNIFFLING]

53
00:03:02,700 --> 00:03:05,700
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

54
00:03:06,267 --> 00:03:09,400
[RICARDO] Sam, it's late,
and you're too young

55
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,500
<i> to be galavanting around
at this hour.</i>

56
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:15,500
<i>I just really want to go
to Tricia's farewell party.</i>

57
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:17,867
<i>Mommy, I haven't failed
any of my subjects.</i>

58
00:03:17,867 --> 00:03:19,567
<i> Come on. Make this my reward.</i>

59
00:03:19,567 --> 00:03:21,567
<i> Oh, Sam, I'm sorry.</i>

60
00:03:22,133 --> 00:03:23,733
<i> Your dad already decided.</i>

61
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:26,167
<i> You heard your mom.</i>

62
00:03:26,167 --> 00:03:28,467
<i>I'm sorry you're going to miss
your friend's party.</i>

63
00:03:30,433 --> 00:03:35,433
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

64
00:03:37,933 --> 00:03:41,433
<i>You're sad again because
Dad wouldn't let you go, huh?</i>

65
00:03:41,433 --> 00:03:44,400
<i>It's because Dad's
being unfair, RJ.</i>

66
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:46,433
<i> I hate him.</i>

67
00:03:46,433 --> 00:03:47,867
<i> You're Dad's responsibility.</i>

68
00:03:48,567 --> 00:03:52,167
<i>And you're my responsibility
because we're family.</i>

69
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,700
<i> Here. This is for you.</i>

70
00:03:57,667 --> 00:03:59,200
<i> What's this for?</i>

71
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:02,033
<i> Just a reminder that
every moment,</i>

72
00:04:02,033 --> 00:04:04,767
<i>we have a responsibility
to our loved ones.</i>

73
00:04:04,767 --> 00:04:06,867
<i>We should always think about
what's best for them,</i>

74
00:04:06,867 --> 00:04:08,900
<i>even when we're busy
doing other things,</i>

75
00:04:08,900 --> 00:04:10,533
because they do the same for us.

76
00:04:10,533 --> 00:04:12,300
[CHUCKLES] Thanks, RJ.

77
00:04:12,300 --> 00:04:18,067
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

78
00:04:24,433 --> 00:04:26,633
<i> "I'll pick you up."</i>

79
00:04:26,633 --> 00:04:28,867
- [KEYPAD CLICKING]
<i> - "I'll get ready."</i>

80
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:34,100
[ISOBEL]<i> Apparently,
</i>Miss Universe is being held here

81
00:04:34,100 --> 00:04:36,000
<i> this year, and, oh...</i>

82
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,333
<i>Well, I'm hoping
they'll invite me.</i>

83
00:04:39,333 --> 00:04:40,633
[MAX GIGGLES]

84
00:04:40,633 --> 00:04:44,267
<i>Not just in the Philippines,
but in the universe, right?</i>

85
00:04:44,267 --> 00:04:46,867
- [ISOBEL GIGGLES]
- [MAX] I'm sure they will.

86
00:04:48,733 --> 00:04:51,467
[RICARDO]<i> That's what I was
</i> telling you earlier, R.J.

87
00:04:51,467 --> 00:04:53,333
<i> You know, I'm confident</i>

88
00:04:53,333 --> 00:04:55,400
<i> you'll be the one to follow
in my footsteps.</i>

89
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:58,567
<i>And, son, when you become
the future Chief of Police,</i>

90
00:04:58,567 --> 00:05:02,033
<i> I'm sure you'll be even
better than me.</i>

91
00:05:02,067 --> 00:05:03,300
[RJ] Thank you, Dad.

92
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:06,633
<i>- Twinkle?
- Sir?</i>

93
00:05:06,633 --> 00:05:08,567
<i> - Dad wants some coffee.
- Ah. Yes, sir.</i>

94
00:05:09,533 --> 00:05:11,167
- [UTENSIL CLINKS]
<i> - Oh!</i>

95
00:05:13,900 --> 00:05:15,033
<i> Damn it!</i>

96
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:17,000
[WOMAN WHISPERING]
<i> Sam, are you there?</i>

97
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,633
<i>- Sam! Sam!
- Shh. Keep it down, guys.</i>

98
00:05:19,833 --> 00:05:20,933
<i>- Sam!
- Wait!</i>

99
00:05:20,933 --> 00:05:22,600
<i>- Come on, let's go!
- Wait.</i>

100
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:24,000
<i>- Come on.
- [SAM GIGGLING]</i>

101
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,733
<i> - Girl, let's go.
- There.</i>

102
00:05:25,733 --> 00:05:27,633
<i> Sam, what took you so long?</i>

103
00:05:27,633 --> 00:05:28,700
<i> Let's go!</i>

104
00:05:28,700 --> 00:05:29,933
[ENGINE REVVING]

105
00:05:29,933 --> 00:05:31,733
[PARTY MUSIC PLAYING]

106
00:05:31,733 --> 00:05:33,100
<i> Whoo!</i>

107
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:34,333
<i>- Sam!
- Hi!</i>

108
00:05:34,367 --> 00:05:35,433
[BOTH SQUEALING]

109
00:05:35,433 --> 00:05:38,067
<i> Oh my God! You made it!</i>

110
00:05:38,633 --> 00:05:40,133
<i> Finally, yes!</i>

111
00:05:40,133 --> 00:05:41,267
<i> Oh, thank you!</i>

112
00:05:41,267 --> 00:05:42,767
<i> Sam, you're a little late.</i>

113
00:05:42,767 --> 00:05:44,533
<i>- Sorry!
- What took you so long?</i>

114
00:05:44,533 --> 00:05:46,333
<i> - My dad.
- Finally, you're here.</i>

115
00:05:46,333 --> 00:05:48,467
<i>- Okay!
- Drink up, girl!</i>

116
00:05:48,467 --> 00:05:49,533
<i> Yes!</i>

117
00:05:50,733 --> 00:05:52,300
<i>- Cheers!
- Cheers!</i>

118
00:05:52,567 --> 00:05:57,867
[PARTY MUSIC CONTINUES]

119
00:05:57,867 --> 00:06:00,233
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

120
00:06:02,667 --> 00:06:09,200
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

121
00:06:09,233 --> 00:06:10,833
[SAM GIGGLING]

122
00:06:10,833 --> 00:06:11,900
<i> Sam?</i>

123
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:13,433
<i> Sam, dear.</i>

124
00:06:15,633 --> 00:06:17,800
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

125
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:19,000
<i> Ricardo!</i>

126
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,500
<i> Sam ran away!</i>

127
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:22,967
<i> That girl is so stubborn.</i>

128
00:06:22,967 --> 00:06:25,000
<i>Find out where your sister
went to party.</i>

129
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,967
<i>- Yes, Dad.
- Dad, I'll take care of it.</i>

130
00:06:27,967 --> 00:06:29,833
<i> I'll bring her home.
She'll be safe.</i>

131
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:34,133
<i>- Whoo!
- Whoo!</i>

132
00:06:34,133 --> 00:06:35,600
<i>- Yeah!
- Let's go!</i>

133
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:37,900
[PARTY CHATTER]

134
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:39,000
<i> Hi, Miss!</i>

135
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:41,367
<i> What's up?</i>

136
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:42,767
<i> Come on, let's dance.</i>

137
00:06:42,767 --> 00:06:44,900
<i> Excuse me,
can you move a bit farther?</i>

138
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:46,433
<i> Whoo! Whoo! Whoo!</i>

139
00:06:46,433 --> 00:06:50,433
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

140
00:06:51,967 --> 00:06:53,167
<i> Sir, one more.</i>

141
00:06:53,167 --> 00:06:57,500
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

142
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:58,600
<i> Why did you leave?</i>

143
00:06:58,600 --> 00:06:59,800
<i> We're still dancing.</i>

144
00:07:00,433 --> 00:07:02,467
<i>Oh, please.
I told you to back off.</i>

145
00:07:02,467 --> 00:07:04,767
<i>Don't be such a snob.
Come on, let's dance.</i>

146
00:07:04,767 --> 00:07:05,767
[MAN 1] Don't play hard to get.

147
00:07:05,767 --> 00:07:07,867
<i> Let me handle this.
She's mine.</i>

148
00:07:07,867 --> 00:07:09,200
<i> Come on. Let's go back there.</i>

149
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:10,833
[SAM] Don't touch me. Back off!

150
00:07:10,833 --> 00:07:13,100
<i>- Come on, Miss.
- Stop it!</i>

151
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:15,667
-<i> Let me go!
- We'll just dance!</i>

152
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:17,100
- [MAN 2]<i> Come on, let's dance!
</i> - Stop!

153
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:18,800
<i>- Stop! Don't touch me!
- Hey!</i>

154
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:21,000
<i> - She already said no!
- RJ!</i>

155
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,967
<i>- Who the hell are you?
- I'm her brother, jerk!</i>

156
00:07:22,967 --> 00:07:24,133
<i> - RJ, no!
- Beat him up!</i>

157
00:07:24,133 --> 00:07:25,300
[BLOWS LANDING]

158
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:26,400
[SAM] Somebody help!

159
00:07:26,400 --> 00:07:28,367
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [WOMEN SHRIEKING]

160
00:07:28,367 --> 00:07:29,267
<i> RJ!</i>

161
00:07:29,267 --> 00:07:30,500
Come on! Is that all you've got?

162
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:31,800
<i>- RJ, that's enough!
- Come on!</i>

163
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:33,367
<i>- That's enough.
- Let's get out of here, Sam.</i>

164
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:38,400
[DOOR OPENS]

165
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:41,400
<i> You'll pay for this!</i>

166
00:07:41,400 --> 00:07:43,133
<i>- Especially you!
- Get out of here!</i>

167
00:07:43,133 --> 00:07:45,000
<i>- Don't ever come back!
- [CAR DOOR OPENS]</i>

168
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,400
<i> Don't ever come back!</i>

169
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:47,800
<i>- You're banned from this bar.
- Leave!</i>

170
00:07:49,300 --> 00:07:50,267
<i> Sam,</i>

171
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,933
<i> why did you sneak out?</i>

172
00:07:52,933 --> 00:07:54,233
<i> RJ,</i>

173
00:07:54,233 --> 00:07:56,733
<i> I just wanted to have fun
with my friends.</i>

174
00:07:57,633 --> 00:08:00,933
<i>Now you know why Dad doesn't
allow you to go on night outs.</i>

175
00:08:01,667 --> 00:08:03,967
<i>You've become a killjoy
just like Dad.</i>

176
00:08:03,967 --> 00:08:04,967
<i> Oh, Sam.</i>

177
00:08:05,733 --> 00:08:07,133
<i> If I hadn't come,</i>

178
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:09,367
<i>what do you think
they'd have done to you?</i>

179
00:08:09,367 --> 00:08:10,667
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

180
00:08:10,667 --> 00:08:11,833
<i> I'm sorry.</i>

181
00:08:11,833 --> 00:08:16,233
<i>Next time,
listen to what Dad says.</i>

182
00:08:16,233 --> 00:08:17,267
<i> Obey him.</i>

183
00:08:18,567 --> 00:08:19,467
<i> Yes, sir.</i>

184
00:08:20,233 --> 00:08:21,767
<i> Come on.</i>

185
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:23,100
<i> Let's go home.</i>

186
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:24,200
<i> Please?</i>

187
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:27,600
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

188
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:28,600
<i> Come on.</i>

189
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:32,533
[CAR APPROACHING]

190
00:08:32,533 --> 00:08:38,633
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

191
00:08:38,633 --> 00:08:40,100
- [MAN 3]<i> Is that him?
</i>- [MAN 1] That's him, bro.

192
00:08:42,567 --> 00:08:44,367
- [RJ]<i> Get in.
</i>- [SAM] Thank you.

193
00:08:46,533 --> 00:08:47,767
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

194
00:08:50,767 --> 00:08:51,867
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

195
00:08:53,667 --> 00:08:54,600
[GUN COCKS]

196
00:08:54,633 --> 00:08:55,733
[GUNSHOTS]

197
00:08:57,733 --> 00:08:58,900
[BODY THUDS]

198
00:09:04,267 --> 00:09:05,333
<i> RJ!</i>

199
00:09:06,500 --> 00:09:07,500
<i> RJ!</i>

200
00:09:09,533 --> 00:09:10,867
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

201
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:13,600
<i> RJ! RJ!</i>

202
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:14,867
<i> RJ!</i> [BREATHING HEAVILY]

203
00:09:14,867 --> 00:09:16,400
<i> Somebody help!</i>

204
00:09:16,400 --> 00:09:17,733
[CRYING] RJ!

205
00:09:17,733 --> 00:09:18,900
<i> RJ!</i>

206
00:09:19,667 --> 00:09:21,733
[SCREAMS] Help!

207
00:09:21,733 --> 00:09:24,033
<i> Somebody help us! RJ!</i>

208
00:09:24,033 --> 00:09:26,367
[CRYING] RJ! RJ, wake up!

209
00:09:26,367 --> 00:09:28,167
<i> RJ!</i>

210
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:30,433
[SCREAMS] Help!

211
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:33,000
<i> RJ!</i>

212
00:09:34,933 --> 00:09:37,033
<i> RJ, wake up! Wake up, RJ!</i>

213
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:39,867
<i> RJ, wake up!</i>

214
00:09:39,867 --> 00:09:42,233
<i> Somebody help!</i>

215
00:09:42,233 --> 00:09:46,133
I'm begging you! Somebody help!

216
00:09:46,133 --> 00:09:49,433
[MUSIC TURNS MELANCHOLIC]

217
00:09:49,433 --> 00:09:52,133
[SNIFFLING, SOBBING]

218
00:09:58,600 --> 00:10:01,067
<i>I'll make them pay
for what they did to you, RJ.</i>

219
00:10:02,067 --> 00:10:04,233
<i> I'm doing my best at NCIA.</i>

220
00:10:05,800 --> 00:10:08,800
<i>I want to solve
your case myself.</i>

221
00:10:11,267 --> 00:10:13,733
<i> I want to solve
all the other cases,</i>

222
00:10:14,833 --> 00:10:17,867
<i>so those criminals
can't hurt anybody else.</i>

223
00:10:19,333 --> 00:10:21,200
<i> As much as I want you back,</i>

224
00:10:22,333 --> 00:10:24,200
I know I can't possibly do that.

225
00:10:26,633 --> 00:10:27,967
<i> But I'll do my best</i>

226
00:10:28,833 --> 00:10:31,100
<i>to make your killer
pay for his crimes.</i>

227
00:10:32,567 --> 00:10:35,633
Because I'm hoping that somehow,

228
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:39,400
<i>it would bring the love back
into our family.</i>

229
00:10:40,867 --> 00:10:47,833
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

230
00:10:56,133 --> 00:10:58,100
- [DISTANT SHOUTING]
<i> - Where are you taking us?!</i>

231
00:10:58,100 --> 00:11:00,167
- [OVERLAPPING SHOUTING]
- Bring 'em in!

232
00:11:00,167 --> 00:11:02,400
- Go!
- Where are we?!

233
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:05,967
[OVERLAPPING SHOUTING]

234
00:11:05,967 --> 00:11:08,133
Let us go!
Let us go!

235
00:11:08,167 --> 00:11:15,100
[OVERLAPPING SHOUTING,
INDISTINCT CHATTER]

236
00:11:18,800 --> 00:11:23,333
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

237
00:11:23,333 --> 00:11:25,967
[BLOWS LAND]

238
00:11:25,967 --> 00:11:27,433
- Come on!
- Come here!

239
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:34,533
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

240
00:11:34,533 --> 00:11:36,800
- [SHOUTING]
- Let us go!

241
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:38,333
So, what happened?

242
00:11:38,333 --> 00:11:40,133
Did you clear
the operating room?

243
00:11:40,133 --> 00:11:42,567
We had a problem with
one of the extracted livers.

244
00:11:42,600 --> 00:11:44,300
But the next one's
in the operating room already.

245
00:11:44,300 --> 00:11:46,100
Tell them to hurry up!

246
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:48,200
We have a delivery tonight!

247
00:11:49,400 --> 00:11:50,667
Bring 'em in!

248
00:11:50,667 --> 00:11:57,267
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

249
00:11:57,267 --> 00:11:58,567
[GRUNTS]

250
00:11:58,567 --> 00:12:00,300
- [SLAMS BODY]
- Hurry up!

251
00:12:04,267 --> 00:12:11,267
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

252
00:12:15,933 --> 00:12:17,133
Boss Django.

253
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:21,000
Hmm?

254
00:12:21,833 --> 00:12:24,233
I think you're losing your edge.

255
00:12:24,233 --> 00:12:26,000
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

256
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,167
What do you mean?

257
00:12:27,167 --> 00:12:28,967
You didn't do Umali's order

258
00:12:28,967 --> 00:12:32,033
and you backed down
from Gabo.

259
00:12:32,033 --> 00:12:35,633
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

260
00:12:35,633 --> 00:12:36,900
[BLOW LANDS]

261
00:12:36,900 --> 00:12:37,833
[BODY THUDS]

262
00:12:37,833 --> 00:12:38,800
Boss!

263
00:12:38,800 --> 00:12:40,133
Back off!

264
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:44,100
Are you messing with me?!

265
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:45,767
How 'bout I wreck your face

266
00:12:45,767 --> 00:12:47,100
so your mother
doesn't recognize you?!

267
00:12:47,100 --> 00:12:48,267
Boss, boss.

268
00:12:48,300 --> 00:12:49,933
I was just joking.
Come on.

269
00:12:49,933 --> 00:12:51,067
[BOTTLE SHATTERS]

270
00:12:53,033 --> 00:12:55,067
I didn't fight Gabo

271
00:12:55,067 --> 00:12:57,200
not because I was scared,

272
00:12:57,200 --> 00:12:58,767
but because I was using my head!

273
00:13:00,833 --> 00:13:02,567
I know Gabo.

274
00:13:02,567 --> 00:13:04,633
Fighting him
is not the right move.

275
00:13:04,633 --> 00:13:09,333
I need him to think
that I'm not a threat anymore.

276
00:13:09,333 --> 00:13:13,367
Then, when his guard's down,
that's when I'll attack!

277
00:13:13,367 --> 00:13:16,100
That's my plan,
you morons!

278
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:20,933
What brings you to the city?

279
00:13:21,667 --> 00:13:23,367
What do you think?

280
00:13:23,367 --> 00:13:24,733
I came here to work!

281
00:13:24,733 --> 00:13:30,367
My wife said
Manila is where the money is.

282
00:13:30,367 --> 00:13:31,700
But you know what?

283
00:13:31,700 --> 00:13:34,167
- I made money back home.
- Mm.

284
00:13:34,167 --> 00:13:36,300
I had a decent job.

285
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:39,833
But she said
it wasn't enough.

286
00:13:39,833 --> 00:13:43,367
Even though
I worked day to night.

287
00:13:44,167 --> 00:13:45,600
It still wasn't enough.

288
00:13:45,600 --> 00:13:48,600
And what's worse is that
I still get the blame.

289
00:13:48,600 --> 00:13:51,467
It was all my fault.

290
00:13:51,467 --> 00:13:53,567
Can you believe it?

291
00:13:53,567 --> 00:13:54,667
Do you get me?

292
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:56,333
Betchay?

293
00:13:56,333 --> 00:13:57,700
Are you crying?

294
00:13:57,700 --> 00:14:00,767
Of course not!
Don't be silly!

295
00:14:00,767 --> 00:14:02,833
- Cheers, man!
- [BOTTLES CLINK]

296
00:14:02,833 --> 00:14:04,167
- Let's finish this!
- [BOTTLES CLINK]

297
00:14:04,167 --> 00:14:06,067
- Alright!
- Yeah!

298
00:14:06,067 --> 00:14:08,200
- No drama!
- Mm!

299
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:12,067
- Let's have a good time!
- Jeez.

300
00:14:12,067 --> 00:14:16,033
Hey!
At least order something!

301
00:14:16,033 --> 00:14:18,367
Hey! Another bucket of beer
for this table!

302
00:14:18,367 --> 00:14:22,133
- Another bucket of beer!
- Enough touching.

303
00:14:22,133 --> 00:14:24,867
You need drinks!
Another bucket over here!

304
00:14:24,867 --> 00:14:26,667
- That table, too.
- Another bucket!

305
00:14:26,667 --> 00:14:29,133
- Over there!
- [BETCHAY SHOUTING]

306
00:14:29,167 --> 00:14:36,133
[COMICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

307
00:14:36,867 --> 00:14:38,000
[BOTTLES CLINK]

308
00:14:42,167 --> 00:14:43,700
- How are we doing tonight?
- Hello.

309
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:45,967
Someone's showing off tonight.

310
00:14:45,967 --> 00:14:49,100
- Take a look.
- [BETCHAY SINGING]

311
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:52,500
Looks like
it's a good night.

312
00:14:52,500 --> 00:14:54,067
[ROSANNA]
Thanks to Betchay.

313
00:14:54,067 --> 00:14:57,433
She's great at
entertaining the customers.

314
00:14:57,433 --> 00:15:00,033
I didn't know
Betchay could be so useful.

315
00:15:00,033 --> 00:15:04,000
[PRISCILLA] You know why
she's showing off tonight?

316
00:15:04,033 --> 00:15:07,200
Rosanna told her to.

317
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:11,300
No, Betchay said
she and Rudy got into a fight.

318
00:15:11,300 --> 00:15:13,900
You should've seen her
when she got here.

319
00:15:13,900 --> 00:15:15,067
She was a mess.

320
00:15:15,067 --> 00:15:17,833
But she got herself together
after I talked to her.

321
00:15:17,833 --> 00:15:19,400
- She's having a blast.
- Whoo!

322
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:24,467
Look at her go,
Madam. [CHUCKLES]

323
00:15:24,467 --> 00:15:26,767
Want to bet?

324
00:15:26,767 --> 00:15:30,567
The night won't end
without her making a mess.

325
00:15:30,567 --> 00:15:33,300
- You got that right.
- For sure.

326
00:15:35,833 --> 00:15:37,233
[VEHICLE APPROACHES]

327
00:15:41,167 --> 00:15:43,767
[ENGINE HUMMING]

328
00:15:44,800 --> 00:15:48,833
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

329
00:15:48,833 --> 00:15:50,833
What is this place?
Where are we?

330
00:15:50,833 --> 00:15:53,167
Gabo.
This is the warehouse.

331
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:58,000
That's where they take
the people they abduct.

332
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,100
That's where they conduct
their operations.

333
00:16:00,100 --> 00:16:01,767
[DABOY] This place is scary.

334
00:16:01,767 --> 00:16:03,733
We're getting ourselves
in trouble, huh?

335
00:16:05,933 --> 00:16:09,767
- [PEOPLE SCREAMING, CRYING]
- Get down! Move it!

336
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:11,900
- Come on!
- Move!

337
00:16:12,733 --> 00:16:14,967
Look!
Those are new victims!

338
00:16:14,967 --> 00:16:19,233
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

339
00:16:19,700 --> 00:16:21,000
[MAN GRUNTS]

340
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,667
[BLOWS, KICK LANDS]

341
00:16:23,667 --> 00:16:25,100
[BODY THUDS]

342
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:26,900
One of them escaped!

343
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:28,967
- Go! Run!
- Hey!

344
00:16:28,967 --> 00:16:30,700
- Shh! Keep it down.
- [MAN] Help!

345
00:16:32,233 --> 00:16:33,700
Help!

346
00:16:33,700 --> 00:16:35,300
- Get in!
- Hurry!

347
00:16:35,300 --> 00:16:37,233
Shut up! Get in!

348
00:16:37,233 --> 00:16:39,233
- Shh!
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

349
00:16:39,233 --> 00:16:41,233
- Shh!
- Calm down!

350
00:16:41,233 --> 00:16:43,133
- We won't hurt you.
- What happened?

351
00:16:43,167 --> 00:16:44,233
We were abducted.

352
00:16:45,467 --> 00:16:47,100
- Someone's coming!
- Hide!

353
00:16:47,100 --> 00:16:49,467
- They're coming!
- Hide! Hide!

354
00:16:49,467 --> 00:16:51,333
- Get down!
- Be quiet!

355
00:16:53,433 --> 00:16:54,700
Where'd he go?

356
00:16:56,067 --> 00:16:57,300
- Hey!
- [THUD]

357
00:16:57,300 --> 00:16:59,967
- [BLOWS LAND]
- The bad guys!

358
00:16:59,967 --> 00:17:00,933
- [KICK LANDS]
- [GOON GRUNTS]

359
00:17:00,933 --> 00:17:04,633
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GRUNTING]

360
00:17:04,633 --> 00:17:06,633
[KICKS LAND]

361
00:17:06,633 --> 00:17:08,200
[BLOW LANDS]

362
00:17:08,200 --> 00:17:09,400
- [BODY THUDS]
- Get him!

363
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:10,933
- [PUNCHES LANDING]
- That's right!

364
00:17:10,933 --> 00:17:12,700
- Alright.
- Gabo.

365
00:17:12,700 --> 00:17:15,333
What do we do?
How will we help them?

366
00:17:15,367 --> 00:17:22,400
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

367
00:17:22,967 --> 00:17:24,267
I have an idea.

368
00:17:24,267 --> 00:17:29,567
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

369
00:17:30,733 --> 00:17:31,867
[GROANS]

370
00:17:31,867 --> 00:17:33,600
[CLUB MUSIC PLAYING
OVER SPEAKERS]

371
00:17:33,600 --> 00:17:34,567
[IBYANG] An hour.

372
00:17:35,233 --> 00:17:37,367
Let's give her an hour.

373
00:17:37,367 --> 00:17:40,700
I'll find a way
to get her kicked out of here.

374
00:17:40,700 --> 00:17:42,067
That's right! Cheers!

375
00:17:42,733 --> 00:17:43,767
[BOTTLES CLINK]

376
00:17:43,767 --> 00:17:50,733
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

377
00:17:56,400 --> 00:17:58,300
- [VOMITS]
- [GRUNTS] My goodness!

378
00:17:58,300 --> 00:18:00,867
Yuck! Let go of me, Betchay!

379
00:18:02,167 --> 00:18:04,400
[BOTTLES BREAKING]

380
00:18:09,167 --> 00:18:10,867
Betchay, what have you done?!

381
00:18:12,733 --> 00:18:16,200
Hey, Betchay!
You better pay for those!

382
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:18,167
It's not my fault!
He pushed me--

383
00:18:18,167 --> 00:18:19,633
It's still your fault!

384
00:18:19,633 --> 00:18:21,967
Rosanna, count all
the broken bottles

385
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:23,133
and have her pay for them.

386
00:18:23,133 --> 00:18:24,533
Why should I pay?

387
00:18:24,533 --> 00:18:26,767
- It's not my fault.
- Matet, get the rag.

388
00:18:26,767 --> 00:18:28,000
This is unfair.

389
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,533
Here. Take this.

390
00:18:30,533 --> 00:18:32,033
Clean up your mess!

391
00:18:32,467 --> 00:18:33,933
Alright, I'm on it.

392
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:36,367
Diana, get back to work.

393
00:18:36,367 --> 00:18:37,900
[ROSANNA]
My goodness, Betchay.

394
00:18:38,533 --> 00:18:40,167
So cranky.

395
00:18:40,867 --> 00:18:43,167
Get back to work, all of you!

396
00:18:44,233 --> 00:18:48,467
[ENGINE HUMMING]

397
00:18:49,067 --> 00:18:51,300
[TEKLA YELPS] What are you
planning to do with us?!

398
00:18:51,300 --> 00:18:53,333
[GABO] Let me go!

399
00:18:54,200 --> 00:18:56,267
- [TOLITS] Get moving!
- [GABO] Let us go!

400
00:18:56,300 --> 00:18:58,600
- I said get moving!
- The cops can't catch us!

401
00:18:58,600 --> 00:18:59,800
Get moving!

402
00:18:59,800 --> 00:19:02,633
- [GABO] Let us go, you scums!
- [IPE] Stop struggling!

403
00:19:02,633 --> 00:19:05,100
[GABO] Let us go, you bastards!

404
00:19:05,967 --> 00:19:07,367
They're from Caloocan!

405
00:19:07,367 --> 00:19:08,333
How old?

406
00:19:08,333 --> 00:19:09,467
In their 20s!

407
00:19:09,467 --> 00:19:10,967
- How many women?
- One.

408
00:19:10,967 --> 00:19:12,333
- How many men?
- Two.

409
00:19:12,333 --> 00:19:14,067
Okay, take them inside
for the operation.

410
00:19:14,067 --> 00:19:15,767
Come on, this way!

411
00:19:15,767 --> 00:19:17,133
- [BINOY] Let us go!
- [TOLITS] Come on!

412
00:19:17,133 --> 00:19:19,033
- [TEKLA YELPS]
- Get moving!

413
00:19:19,033 --> 00:19:21,167
[TEKLA YELPS] Ow!

414
00:19:21,167 --> 00:19:23,267
[WOMAN] What are you
going to do to us?

415
00:19:23,267 --> 00:19:24,700
Stop struggling!

416
00:19:24,700 --> 00:19:25,733
Get moving!

417
00:19:25,733 --> 00:19:27,533
Hurry up!

418
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:29,533
Come here!

419
00:19:29,533 --> 00:19:30,467
[GABO] Let us go!

420
00:19:30,467 --> 00:19:32,333
[TEKLA] Let me go!

421
00:19:32,333 --> 00:19:34,467
Aah! Where are you taking us?!

422
00:19:34,467 --> 00:19:36,200
- [TEKLA] Stop!
- [GABO] Let us go!

423
00:19:36,200 --> 00:19:38,100
Come on! This way!

424
00:19:39,067 --> 00:19:40,600
- Here they are.
- [GABO] You bastards!

425
00:19:40,600 --> 00:19:41,967
Boss! Boss!

426
00:19:41,967 --> 00:19:43,933
Why are there only three?

427
00:19:43,933 --> 00:19:46,000
Sorry, boss.
It's been tough.

428
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:47,900
There are cops
all over the streets,

429
00:19:47,900 --> 00:19:49,000
so we couldn't move freely.

430
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:50,533
It's been really tough lately,
Boss.

431
00:19:50,533 --> 00:19:52,000
We're lucky we even managed
to pick these three up.

432
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:53,400
Where'd you get them?

433
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:55,933
Caloocan. They were dancing
at a bar.

434
00:19:55,933 --> 00:19:56,867
Let me see!

435
00:19:56,867 --> 00:19:58,033
[TEKLA WHIMPERS]

436
00:19:58,033 --> 00:20:00,500
[BINOY] Please let us go!

437
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:02,300
[TEKLA WHIMPERING]

438
00:20:03,733 --> 00:20:04,667
[TEKLA GRUNTS]

439
00:20:04,667 --> 00:20:07,633
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

440
00:20:07,633 --> 00:20:08,933
Let me go!

441
00:20:08,933 --> 00:20:09,933
Shut up!

442
00:20:09,933 --> 00:20:11,033
[MEN SCREAMING]

443
00:20:11,733 --> 00:20:14,067
[MAN] Okay, get started.

444
00:20:14,067 --> 00:20:21,033
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

445
00:20:21,033 --> 00:20:22,567
They're pretty young.

446
00:20:23,633 --> 00:20:25,400
I bet their organs are
still healthy.

447
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:29,067
They should fetch a good price
from foreign buyers.

448
00:20:30,433 --> 00:20:31,700
So what are you waiting for?

449
00:20:31,700 --> 00:20:32,867
Check them out.

450
00:20:32,867 --> 00:20:34,667
- Check what?
- You animals!

451
00:20:34,700 --> 00:20:36,833
So this is what you do
to helpless people?

452
00:20:37,933 --> 00:20:39,533
You turn them into a business!

453
00:20:39,533 --> 00:20:41,000
[TEKLA]
You really have no mercy!

454
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:43,467
Don't you ever think that
every person here has a family

455
00:20:43,467 --> 00:20:45,567
and you're destroying
their future?!

456
00:20:45,567 --> 00:20:47,533
We don't care!

457
00:20:48,033 --> 00:20:51,267
We'll do whatever it takes
to make money.

458
00:20:51,267 --> 00:20:52,900
You're too lazy to find
a decent job,

459
00:20:52,900 --> 00:20:55,567
so you'd rather kill people
to make a living!

460
00:20:55,567 --> 00:20:59,100
There's nothing you can do
now that you're here.

461
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:01,933
We're going to
butcher you alive.

462
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:03,567
That's where you're wrong.

463
00:21:07,900 --> 00:21:09,467
We'll be the ones
butchering you.

464
00:21:09,867 --> 00:21:11,567
[GRUNTING]

465
00:21:11,567 --> 00:21:13,900
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

466
00:21:13,900 --> 00:21:19,667
[GRUNTING]

467
00:21:26,033 --> 00:21:32,933
- [THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [GRUNTING]

468
00:21:36,867 --> 00:21:39,733
[GRUNTING]

469
00:21:41,067 --> 00:21:42,833
[SLINGSHOT TWANGS]

470
00:21:44,433 --> 00:21:45,567
[SLINGSHOT TWANGS]

471
00:21:45,567 --> 00:21:48,933
[GRUNTING]

472
00:21:49,133 --> 00:21:54,633
[SLINGSHOT TWANGING]

473
00:21:56,333 --> 00:21:58,200
- [GRUNTS]
- [SLINGSHOT TWANGS]

474
00:21:58,200 --> 00:22:04,100
- [THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [GRUNTING]

475
00:22:04,100 --> 00:22:05,700
- [THUD]
- [SLINGSHOT TWANGS]

476
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:15,200
[GRUNTING]

477
00:22:15,200 --> 00:22:16,400
[SLINGSHOT TWANGS]

478
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:25,967
- [SLINGSHOT TWANGS]
- [GRUNTING]

479
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:31,533
[KICK LANDS]

480
00:22:31,533 --> 00:22:33,400
[MAN GRUNTING]

481
00:22:33,400 --> 00:22:34,867
[BLOWS LAND]

482
00:22:34,867 --> 00:22:36,233
- [BONES CRACK]
- [MAN GRUNTS]

483
00:22:36,233 --> 00:22:37,467
[BLOWS LAND]

484
00:22:39,733 --> 00:22:40,900
[CRASHES]

485
00:22:42,433 --> 00:22:44,167
- [KICK LANDS]
- [CRASHES]

486
00:22:44,167 --> 00:22:46,533
[SLINGSHOT TWANGING]

487
00:22:50,600 --> 00:22:53,100
- [WHIMPERS]
- [KICK LANDS]

488
00:22:53,100 --> 00:22:54,667
- [MAN GROANS]
- [GUN CLICKS]

489
00:22:58,433 --> 00:22:59,600
Where's Gabo?

490
00:23:02,767 --> 00:23:04,267
Where's Gabo?!

491
00:23:05,100 --> 00:23:07,467
[SLINGSHOT TWANGING]

492
00:23:11,967 --> 00:23:13,133
[BODY THUDS]

493
00:23:14,233 --> 00:23:18,167
[MUSIC BUILDS]

494
00:23:24,667 --> 00:23:28,167
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

495
00:23:28,167 --> 00:23:29,900
[WOMEN SCREAMING]

496
00:23:42,900 --> 00:23:43,967
Mister Babot.

497
00:23:43,967 --> 00:23:44,933
Mister Babot.

498
00:23:45,567 --> 00:23:46,667
Mister Babot.

499
00:23:48,233 --> 00:23:49,267
[BABOT] Gabo?

500
00:23:50,100 --> 00:23:51,567
- Help us, Gabo.
- [GABO EXHALES SHARPLY]

501
00:23:52,033 --> 00:23:54,033
Mister Babot, you're safe now.

502
00:23:54,033 --> 00:23:56,200
Let's go separately!
We'll take the back!

503
00:23:56,233 --> 00:23:57,233
- Let's go!
- Come on!

504
00:23:57,233 --> 00:23:58,567
- [BINOY] Come on!
- [TEKLA] Let's go!

505
00:23:59,600 --> 00:24:00,567
Hurry!

506
00:24:02,067 --> 00:24:03,800
Thank you, Gabo.

507
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:05,433
- [GABO BREATHES HEAVILY]
- Thank you...

508
00:24:06,667 --> 00:24:07,700
Gabo!

509
00:24:07,700 --> 00:24:08,733
Gabo, let's go!

510
00:24:08,733 --> 00:24:10,567
The other might catch us here!

511
00:24:10,567 --> 00:24:12,133
- [TEKLA] Gabo!
- Help all the victims!

512
00:24:12,133 --> 00:24:13,400
- [TEKLA] Gabo!
- Carry them!

513
00:24:13,400 --> 00:24:14,633
- Let's save them.
- Let's go!

514
00:24:14,633 --> 00:24:15,667
Let's go, come on!

515
00:24:15,667 --> 00:24:16,833
[TEKLA] Bring everyone!

516
00:24:17,300 --> 00:24:18,833
[GRUNTS] Careful.

517
00:24:18,833 --> 00:24:20,333
- Hold onto me.
- Thank you, Gabo.

518
00:24:20,333 --> 00:24:21,833
- Where to?
- This way!

519
00:24:23,167 --> 00:24:24,467
Hurry up! Come on!

520
00:24:25,833 --> 00:24:27,033
Come on, let's go!

521
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:30,167
[BINOY] Hurry!

522
00:24:30,167 --> 00:24:31,167
This way.

523
00:24:36,300 --> 00:24:38,033
- Hurry! They might catch us!
- Come on!

524
00:24:38,033 --> 00:24:39,333
We might get caught!

525
00:24:43,133 --> 00:24:46,200
I'm really against her
working here.

526
00:24:47,033 --> 00:24:48,833
Not only did she make a mess,

527
00:24:49,533 --> 00:24:51,300
she also smashed
the beer bottles.

528
00:24:51,300 --> 00:24:53,233
What is her problem?

529
00:24:53,233 --> 00:24:54,567
She doesn't stop talking.

530
00:24:54,567 --> 00:24:56,833
If you have a problem at home,

531
00:24:57,333 --> 00:24:59,033
don't bring it to work.

532
00:24:59,033 --> 00:25:00,167
[MATET] That's right.

533
00:25:02,400 --> 00:25:04,200
And she's always talking back.

534
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:05,567
- [LOUD THUD]
- Hey.

535
00:25:06,067 --> 00:25:08,367
If you have a problem with me,

536
00:25:08,567 --> 00:25:09,700
say it to my face.

537
00:25:09,700 --> 00:25:11,033
Fine!

538
00:25:11,033 --> 00:25:13,967
I have a problem with you.
You know what, huh?

539
00:25:14,900 --> 00:25:16,600
I can get you
kicked out of here.

540
00:25:16,600 --> 00:25:18,800
How and why will you do that?

541
00:25:18,800 --> 00:25:22,533
Paquito's the only one
who can kick me out of here.

542
00:25:22,533 --> 00:25:25,067
- And why is that?
- Because he's my boss.

543
00:25:25,067 --> 00:25:26,633
I'm Paquito's wife.

544
00:25:26,633 --> 00:25:29,200
- [BETCHAY LAUGHS]
- So I'm your boss too!

545
00:25:29,500 --> 00:25:32,133
She's saying he's her wife
when they're not even married!

546
00:25:32,133 --> 00:25:34,400
[LAUGHING MANICALLY]

547
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:41,167
[BOTH LAUGHING]

548
00:25:41,200 --> 00:25:42,500
[SMACKS]

549
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:46,933
- Don't fight back!
- [TISSUES SMACKS]

550
00:25:47,400 --> 00:25:49,433
- That's enough!
- Stop!

551
00:25:50,033 --> 00:25:51,633
Hey!

552
00:25:54,133 --> 00:25:56,533
[ROSANNA] My gosh!
Stop it, you two!

553
00:25:56,533 --> 00:25:57,633
[GROANS]

554
00:25:57,633 --> 00:25:58,933
[IBYANG SCREAMS]

555
00:25:58,933 --> 00:26:02,300
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

556
00:26:02,300 --> 00:26:03,467
That's enough!

557
00:26:03,900 --> 00:26:05,000
Stop it!

558
00:26:05,733 --> 00:26:07,533
I said stop! That's enough!

559
00:26:08,067 --> 00:26:09,067
Enough!

560
00:26:09,567 --> 00:26:11,967
I said stop! Stop it!

561
00:26:11,967 --> 00:26:13,567
[ROSANNA] Ibyang, enough!

562
00:26:13,567 --> 00:26:15,400
- Enough! Stop!
- Come here!

563
00:26:15,800 --> 00:26:16,767
Stop!

564
00:26:17,833 --> 00:26:20,100
Ibyang! Go home!

565
00:26:20,100 --> 00:26:22,933
Romy, take her home!

566
00:26:22,933 --> 00:26:24,000
Go home!

567
00:26:24,800 --> 00:26:26,000
Bleh!

568
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:27,400
- You!
- Enough!

569
00:26:28,467 --> 00:26:31,033
Paquito, look!
She's not listening to you!

570
00:26:31,033 --> 00:26:33,000
- Stop it!
- [BETCHAY] Take her home!

571
00:26:37,267 --> 00:26:39,133
- It's Mister Babot!
- We're almost there.

572
00:26:39,133 --> 00:26:41,633
- Careful, Mister Babot.
- Mister Babot is back!

573
00:26:41,633 --> 00:26:44,100
- [MAN] Abet, call Anthony!
- Call Mister Babot's wife!

574
00:26:44,133 --> 00:26:45,933
[BINOY] We're almost there.
We're here.

575
00:26:45,933 --> 00:26:47,400
Mister Babot and the others
are here!

576
00:26:47,400 --> 00:26:49,767
- Where is he?
- [CRIES] Come on, dear.

577
00:26:49,767 --> 00:26:52,167
- Pa...
- Thank God he's back.

578
00:26:52,167 --> 00:26:53,467
[SOBS]

579
00:26:53,467 --> 00:26:55,100
He's here. Miss Celing!

580
00:26:55,100 --> 00:26:57,233
- Pa!
- [SOBS] Papa!

581
00:26:57,233 --> 00:26:59,500
- [CELING] Hold on.
- [KIDS] Pa!

582
00:27:01,033 --> 00:27:02,367
[GABO] Mister Babot is here.

583
00:27:02,367 --> 00:27:03,933
[INDISTINCT CRY]

584
00:27:03,933 --> 00:27:08,767
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

585
00:27:08,767 --> 00:27:10,900
- [WOMAN] My husband...
- Pa!

586
00:27:23,200 --> 00:27:26,867
Gabo, thank you
for saving my husband.

587
00:27:27,400 --> 00:27:28,667
If it weren't for you,

588
00:27:28,667 --> 00:27:30,867
he's probably gone now.

589
00:27:30,867 --> 00:27:32,067
[BABOT] Gabo.

590
00:27:32,967 --> 00:27:36,067
Thank you for saving us.

591
00:27:36,667 --> 00:27:37,733
If you hadn't been there,

592
00:27:37,733 --> 00:27:39,700
we would've been in danger.

593
00:27:40,667 --> 00:27:42,767
I will never forget
about your kindness.

594
00:27:42,767 --> 00:27:45,633
I will repay you
for the rest of my life.

595
00:27:45,633 --> 00:27:48,100
- [MAN 1] Thank you, Gabo.
- [WOMAN 1] Thank you.

596
00:27:48,100 --> 00:27:50,300
Thank you to you
and your friends.

597
00:27:50,333 --> 00:27:51,867
Thank you.

598
00:27:53,500 --> 00:27:54,667
Don't worry.

599
00:27:55,667 --> 00:27:57,200
We only did the right thing.

600
00:27:57,200 --> 00:27:59,700
- Thank you.
- Thank you, Gabo!

601
00:27:59,700 --> 00:28:01,000
Thank you so much, Gabo.

602
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:02,467
- [KID CRIES] Thank you.
- [TEKLA] Hush now.

603
00:28:02,467 --> 00:28:04,367
[BINOY] Focus on recovery.
Stay safe.

604
00:28:04,367 --> 00:28:06,533
[WOMAN 2]
Thank you for helping us.

605
00:28:08,733 --> 00:28:09,933
[BINOY] Be careful.

606
00:28:10,133 --> 00:28:11,433
[WOMAN 3] Are you hurt anywhere?

607
00:28:11,633 --> 00:28:12,967
- [MAN 2] No, I'm fine.
- [MAN 3] Were you hurt?

608
00:28:12,967 --> 00:28:16,267
Gabo, since we were able to
save Mister Babot

609
00:28:16,267 --> 00:28:17,800
and the others,

610
00:28:18,000 --> 00:28:19,867
I think we deserve
to have some drinks.

611
00:28:19,867 --> 00:28:20,767
Oh!

612
00:28:20,767 --> 00:28:22,700
That was an intense experience.

613
00:28:22,733 --> 00:28:24,867
I really thought we
were going to die.

614
00:28:24,867 --> 00:28:25,900
Me, too.

615
00:28:25,900 --> 00:28:27,133
Yeah, Gabo.

616
00:28:27,133 --> 00:28:29,700
Why don't we drink
to our neighbor's safety?

617
00:28:29,700 --> 00:28:31,200
- Yeah.
- [CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

618
00:28:31,533 --> 00:28:33,867
- Let's go, let's go.
- Come on.

619
00:28:33,867 --> 00:28:35,100
You coming, Gabo?

620
00:28:36,633 --> 00:28:38,067
- Yeah.
- Alright!

621
00:28:38,067 --> 00:28:39,433
- Let's go!
- Yes!

622
00:28:39,800 --> 00:28:41,833
[GROANS] My body hurts.

623
00:28:41,833 --> 00:28:46,833
[HAPPY MUSIC PLAYS]

624
00:28:47,633 --> 00:28:49,100
This Tuesday...

625
00:28:49,100 --> 00:28:52,633
<i> We can get involved in
</i>Ma'am Sam's investigation, too.

626
00:28:52,633 --> 00:28:54,833
<i>If we get in trouble,
just forget we're ever friends.</i>

627
00:28:54,833 --> 00:28:57,633
<i> You really came here
to face the consequences?</i>

628
00:28:57,667 --> 00:29:00,467
<i> The case is getting
more and more complicated</i>

629
00:29:00,467 --> 00:29:01,867
<i> because of you, Jacinto.</i>

630
00:29:01,867 --> 00:29:04,367
<i> We'd probably be better off
without you.</i>

631
00:29:04,367 --> 00:29:07,667
<i>Gabo, promise me
you'll never do anything bad.</i>

632
00:29:08,800 --> 00:29:09,867
<i> Y-yes, Pa.</i>

633
00:29:09,867 --> 00:29:11,333
<i> I promise you.</i>

634
00:29:12,100 --> 00:29:14,233
<i> We'll buy so much stuff!</i>

635
00:29:14,233 --> 00:29:15,933
<i> - Give me your bag!
- Help!</i>

636
00:29:15,933 --> 00:29:17,900
- [MOTORCYCLE REVS]
<i> - Help!</i>

637
00:29:17,900 --> 00:29:19,500
<i> - This is a stickup!
- Give me that!</i>

638
00:29:19,500 --> 00:29:21,133
- [MOTORCYCLE REVS]
- [SOBBING]

639
00:29:21,133 --> 00:29:22,233
[TIRES SCREECH]

640
00:29:22,233 --> 00:29:25,100
- [MOTORCYCLE REVVING]
- [YELLING]

641
00:29:27,567 --> 00:29:29,500
<i> Grandma!</i>

642
00:29:30,400 --> 00:29:32,600
<i> Coco Martin's Sigabo!</i>
